{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>These you shall offer to YHWH at your appointed seasons.</b> A fixed matter as an obligation." "<b>Besides your vows.</b> If you come to vow offerings on the festival, it is a mitzvah in your hand — or vows or freewill offerings that you vowed all the year, bring them on the festival, lest it be hard for him to go back and go up to Jerusalem and offer his vows, and he be found to transgress 'do not delay'."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:13.719117937Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}